{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T06:40:29.725Z","ordinal":708,"type":"compacted","payload":{"message":"","replacement_history":[{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0566a-21fd-7ba3-958a-c7bef5c8a4c9","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"지금 압축 codec 실험에 cd3 있지?\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0566a-2136-7ae1-9cbf-d13ddf0abef7","create_time":1788156191.2290053,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0566a-9b82-7e63-8c33-84111f5ac742","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"지금 압축 codec 실험에 cd3 있지? 컨테이너 내 환경에서 말하는거야\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0566a-9b6b-7802-ba32-41ab2804dcd6","create_time":1788156222.338213,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0566c-43d0-78c2-9a42-c32539fd80a9","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"기존 cd3을 모두 날리고 CD3\\_PACKED20X3\\_GH200\\_CANDIDATE.patch 이 cd3 버전으로 패치해줘.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0566c-43b9-7062-a633-7c37fa749bc2","create_time":1788156330.9606316,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a05674-f40b-7252-af1d-39367d92e444","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"이 버전으로 다시 압축(weight, fused, kv)해서 p4flat과 비교해줘\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a05674-f3f7-7842-be68-e8f4c7b8f6bb","create_time":1788156900.3635087,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0567f-c44c-73c2-96b3-98bd6fa2fc85","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"아래 응답 기반으로 개선해봐.\n\n\n\n보여. 특히 CD3 fused가 decode-bound라는 신호가 강해.\n\n- O: N `64→128`인데 CD3는 `0.152→0.154 ms`\n- Down: `0.473→0.474 ms`\n\nGEMM 양이 두 배가 됐는데 시간이 거의 그대로라는 건, Tensor Core 계산보다 매 K-tile의 CD3 복호화가 지배한다는 뜻이야.\n\n가장 먼저 시도할 건 3-bit code loader야. 현재 CD3는 16개 code의 48bit를 thread마다 `uint8` 6회로 읽어 조립한다. P4Flat은 16개 4-bit code를 정렬된 `uint64` 한 번으로 읽는다.\n\nCD3도 크기를 늘리지 않고 다음처럼 바꿀 수 있어:\n\n- 기존: `6 × uint8 load`\n- 후보: 정렬된 `2 × uint32 load` 후 shift\n- 저장 형식과 압축률은 그대로\n- 마지막 thread도 타일 범위를 넘지 않음\n- B200과 GH200 모두 좋아질 가능성이 있음\n\n두 번째로 반드시 확인할 건 fused exception 처리야. Weight 압축률로 역산하면 CD3 exception이 대략 0.9% 수준이야. 만약 fused GEMM 뒤에서 exception마다 rank-1 보정을 한다면 GateUp에는 수백만 개가 생겨서 지금의 `+0.27~0.32 ms` 열세를 설명할 수 있어. 이 경우에는:\n\n- GEMM 후 correction 금지\n- Packed20 exception을 A shared-memory tile에 먼저 적용\n- 그 뒤 MMA 실행\n\n으로 바꿔야 해.\n\n그다음이 `TileM/TileN`, 128-thread/256-thread, decode–MMA overlap 조정이야. 하지만 loader와 exception 경로를 고치기 전에는 타일 튜닝 효과가 묻힐 가능성이 크다.\n\n다만 GH 서버의 `logs/benchmarks/packed20x3_cd3_20260831/`와 fused CUDA 소스는 이 서버에 없어서 exception 처리가 실제로 어떤 방식인지는 아직 확인하지 못했어. 우선순위는:\n\n1. `6×U8 → 2×U32` loader 실험\n2. exception-only 시간 분해 및 shared-memory 선반영 확인\n3. fused 타일/파이프라인 튜닝\n\n1번부터 패치 후보를 만드는 게 가장 좋아 보여.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0567f-c435-7760-b7a1-27aeac8f9fbc","create_time":1788157609.0363293,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a05680-37ab-7db0-85c4-10b1fecd2b20","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"보여. 특히 CD3 fused가 decode-bound라는 신호가 강해.\n\n- O: N `64→128`인데 CD3는 `0.152→0.154 ms`\n- Down: `0.473→0.474 ms`\n\nGEMM 양이 두 배가 됐는데 시간이 거의 그대로라는 건, Tensor Core 계산보다 매 K-tile의 CD3 복호화가 지배한다는 뜻이야.\n\n가장 먼저 시도할 건 3-bit code loader야. 현재 CD3는 16개 code의 48bit를 thread마다 `uint8` 6회로 읽어 조립한다. P4Flat은 16개 4-bit code를 정렬된 `uint64` 한 번으로 읽는다.\n\nCD3도 크기를 늘리지 않고 다음처럼 바꿀 수 있어:\n\n- 기존: `6 × uint8 load`\n- 후보: 정렬된 `2 × uint32 load` 후 shift\n- 저장 형식과 압축률은 그대로\n- 마지막 thread도 타일 범위를 넘지 않음\n- B200과 GH200 모두 좋아질 가능성이 있음\n\n두 번째로 반드시 확인할 건 fused exception 처리야. Weight 압축률로 역산하면 CD3 exception이 대략 0.9% 수준이야. 만약 fused GEMM 뒤에서 exception마다 rank-1 보정을 한다면 GateUp에는 수백만 개가 생겨서 지금의 `+0.27~0.32 ms` 열세를 설명할 수 있어. 이 경우에는:\n\n- GEMM 후 correction 금지\n- Packed20 exception을 A shared-memory tile에 먼저 적용\n- 그 뒤 MMA 실행\n\n으로 바꿔야 해.\n\n그다음이 `TileM/TileN`, 128-thread/256-thread, decode–MMA overlap 조정이야. 하지만 loader와 exception 경로를 고치기 전에는 타일 튜닝 효과가 묻힐 가능성이 크다.\n\n다만 GH 서버의 `logs/benchmarks/packed20x3_cd3_20260831/`와 fused CUDA 소스는 이 서버에 없어서 exception 처리가 실제로 어떤 방식인지는 아직 확인하지 못했어. 우선순위는:\n\n1. `6×U8 → 2×U32` loader 실험\n2. exception-only 시간 분해 및 shared-memory 선반영 확인\n3. fused 타일/파이프라인 튜닝\n\n1번부터 패치 후보를 만드는 게 가장 좋아 보여.\n\n\n\n\\--------------------\n\n이 응답 어떻게 생각해? 충분히 일리 있는 거야?\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a05680-3794-70c2-b85c-49f072cd4d1e","create_time":1788157638.5718975,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a05683-9c6f-7fe3-a955-6b5329c7bc35","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"아래 의견은 어떻게 생각해? 다른 codex로부터 받은 결과야.\n\n\n\nGH Codex 분석이 더 정확해. 내가 fused 구현을 보지 못한 상태에서 추정한 두 부분은 현재 코드에는 해당하지 않아.\n\n다만 우선순위 2번의 “overlap”보다 먼저 더 간단한 개선이 보여.\n\n현재 CD3는 code `7` 자체가 exception 표시야. 따라서 별도 mask가 필요 없어:\n```csharp\nexception_exp[tile_position] = exponent;   // 위치는 유일하므로 atomic 불필요\n\nexponent = code == 7\n    ? exception_exp[tile_position]\n    : base + code;\n```\n\n이렇게 하면 매 K-tile마다 수행하는:\n\n- mask 초기화\n- shared atomic\n- mask 확인\n- 불필요한 동기화 하나\n\n를 제거할 수 있어. stale map 값도 `code==7`일 때만 읽으므로 문제가 없다. Packed20에 이미 `tile_position + exponent`가 들어 있어 포맷 변경도 필요 없다.\n\n추천 순서는 다음이야.\n\n1. exception-map 전체를 끈 timing-only A/B\n2. `code==7` 기반 direct exponent map 구현\n3. 여전히 느리면 shared code 추출을 값별 byte load에서 chunk별 `2×uint32` 로드로 변경\n4. 그다음 이전 WGMMA와 다음 exception decode overlap\n5. standalone decoder의 `2×uint32` 적용\n\n특히 fused가 현재 값마다 shared byte를 1\\~2회 읽는다면, 4096개 값 전체에서 상당한 instruction이 발생한다. 16개 code를 48-bit 단위로 register에 한 번 캐싱할 수 있다면 exception 다음으로 유력하다.\n\n마지막 chunk 문제도 GH Codex 말이 맞는데, 우리가 말한 정렬 방식이면 안전해. 마지막 thread는 `base=1530`, `base&~3=1528`이고 두 word가 `1528..1535`를 읽으므로 1536-byte 타일을 넘지 않는다.\n\n현재 가장 타당한 다음 실험은 `exception off → direct map` 두 단계야. 이걸 먼저 승인하면 원인과 개선 효과를 가장 깨끗하게 분리할 수 있어.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a05683-9c56-78a2-84ba-3170083dccf0","create_time":1788157860.9751196,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a05687-9cdd-7031-bc5c-8d66c88b2ab4","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"아래 응답은 어떻게 생각해?\n\n\n\nGH Codex가 맞습니다. 제가 TP3의 escape 의미를 CD3에 잘못 적용했습니다.\n\n- CD3는 정상 `code=0…7`을 모두 사용합니다.\n- exception은 임시로 `code=0`이라 정상 delta 0과 구분되지 않습니다. [소스](/home/pjw7200/project/tiered-serve/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/tp3_cd3.cu)\n- packed20x3 패치는 code 규칙을 바꾸지 않습니다. [패치](/home/pjw7200/project/tiered-serve/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/CD3_PACKED20X3_GH200_CANDIDATE.patch)\n\n따라서:\n\n1. `code7 sentinel`은 현 포맷에 바로 적용 불가\n2. exponent map에서 atomic만 없애도 exception 여부를 판별할 mask가 여전히 필요\n3. 제 direct-map 제안은 폐기해야 합니다\n\n다만 `code7 sentinel` 실험은 이미 B200에서 사실상 검증했습니다. Escape7은 exception이 85.6% 증가하고 decode가 11.11% 느려졌습니다. [결과](/home/pjw7200/project/tiered-serve/benchmarks/research_handoff/tp3_cd3_gh200/ESCAPE7_INLINE_REPORT.md) Packed20을 유지하며 code7을 예약하면 B200 KV 기준 예상 압축률도 약 `1.3347x`까지 떨어져 P4Flat `1.3259x`와 차이가 거의 없어집니다. 우선순위 3번은 낮추는 게 맞습니다.\n\n더 적합한 다음 후보는 포맷을 유지하는 sparse warp-owner 방식입니다.\n\n- Packed20 entry는 tile position 순으로 정렬됨\n- 각 warp가 자기 위치 범위의 exception만 읽음\n- entry를 warp에 broadcast하고, 해당 값을 소유한 lane이 자기 A register를 직접 수정\n- dense mask 초기화, shared atomic, 16개 값마다 mask lookup 제거\n- 압축률과 Packed20 포맷은 그대로 유지\n\n권장 순서는:\n\n1. exception-off A/B로 최대 개선폭 측정\n2. mask 초기화·atomic·barrier를 각각 분해\n3. `sparse warp-owner` 구현\n4. shared-code register caching\n5. decode–WGMMA overlap\n\n즉 원인 가설은 아직 유효하지만, 해결책은 `code7 sentinel`이 아니라 **exception 위치 정보를 sparse하게 owner lane으로 직접 전달하는 것**으로 수정해야 합니다.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a05687-9cb9-7443-a4e9-50f26e0fee5c","create_time":1788158123.2298546,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0568c-4a1c-7613-bf0b-98e13ff1988b","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<skills_instructions>\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/home/ubuntu/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r1` = `/home/ubuntu/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: r0/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including 'you,' 'your,' 'this app,' or 'this coding agent' when they refer to Codex—and for OpenAI APIs/products and ChatGPT Work. Also use for model choice/migration, prompting, SDKs, Responses, Realtime, agents, evals, and Chat/Work/Codex comparisons. Do not use for generic app/software tasks that merely mention Codex. (file: r0/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-creator: Create and scaffold plugin directories for Codex with a required `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, optional plugin folders/files, valid manifest defaults, and personal-marketplace entries by default. Use when Codex needs to create a new personal plugin, add optional plugin structure, generate or update marketplace entries for plugin ordering and availability metadata, or update an existing local plugin during development with the CLI-driven cachebuster and reinstall flow. (file: r0/plugin-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r0/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: r0/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-management:plugin-management: Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit from an external app, account, service, or data source that available tools cannot access. (file: r1/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md)\n</skills_instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<permissions instructions>\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `danger-full-access`: No filesystem sandboxing - all commands are permitted. Network access is enabled.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\n</permissions instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<collaboration_mode># Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `<collaboration_mode>...</collaboration_mode>` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nIn Default mode, strongly prefer making reasonable assumptions and executing the user's request rather than stopping to ask questions. If you absolutely must ask a question because the answer cannot be discovered from local context and a reasonable assumption would be risky, ask the user directly with a concise plain-text question. Never write a multiple choice question as a textual assistant message.\n</collaboration_mode>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<apps_instructions>\n## Apps (Connectors)\nApps (Connectors) can be explicitly triggered in user messages in the format `[$app-name](app://{connector_id})`. Apps can also be implicitly triggered as long as the context suggests usage of available apps.\nAn app is equivalent to a set of MCP tools within the `codex_apps` MCP.\nAn installed app's MCP tools are either provided to you already, or can be lazy-loaded through the `tool_search` tool. If `tool_search` is available, the apps that are searchable by `tools_search` will be listed by it.\nDo not additionally call list_mcp_resources or list_mcp_resource_templates for apps.\n</apps_instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<plugins_instructions>\n## Plugins\nA plugin is a local bundle of skills, MCP servers, and apps.\n### How to use plugins\n- Skill naming: If a plugin contributes skills, those skill entries are prefixed with `plugin_name:` in the Skills list.\n- MCP naming: Plugin-provided MCP tools keep standard MCP identifiers such as `mcp__server__tool`; use tool provenance to tell which plugin they come from.\n- Trigger rules: If the user explicitly names a plugin, prefer capabilities associated with that plugin for that turn.\n- Relationship to capabilities: Plugins are not invoked directly. Use their underlying skills, MCP tools, and app tools to help solve the task.\n- Relevance: Determine what a plugin can help with from explicit user mention or from the plugin-associated skills, MCP tools, and apps exposed elsewhere in this turn.\n- Missing/blocked: If the user requests a plugin that does not have relevant callable capabilities for the task, say so briefly and continue with the best fallback.\n</plugins_instructions>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a05689-f1bb-7113-b755-98c4c0fabf30","content_item_kinds":["host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions","apps.instructions","plugins.usage_instructions"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0568c-4a1c-7613-bf0b-98f71ebf25ac","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"You are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: <recipient>\nSender: <author>\nPayload:\n<payload text>\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a05689-f1bb-7113-b755-98c4c0fabf30","content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.usage_hint"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0568c-4a1c-7613-bf0b-99096d08436d","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<multi_agent_mode>Any earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.</multi_agent_mode>"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a05689-f1bb-7113-b755-98c4c0fabf30","content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"]}},{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0568c-4a1c-7613-bf0b-991c40d29027","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<recommended_plugins>\nHere is a list of plugins that are available but not installed.\n\n- Airtable (airtable@openai-curated-remote)\n- Alpaca (alpaca@openai-curated-remote)\n- Apollo.io (apollo@openai-curated-remote)\n- Spotify (app-68de829bf7648191acd70a907364c67c@openai-curated-remote)\n- AllTrails (app-68f1afc5a6008191a701eaaab428816c@openai-curated-remote)\n- Instacart (app-691eab1e001081919e57189f8b2f03bc@openai-curated-remote)\n- Apple Music (app-6938a94a61d881918ef32cb999ff937c@openai-curated-remote)